// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// A root with no prefix of its own that names an included file's types with a
// fully-qualified `::`-form.
//
// Two things are pinned here.  First, identity: nothing declared in this file
// may pick up `common.idl`'s `meridian.example`, so `Depot::Bay` is
// `IDL:Depot/Bay:1.0` while `Freight::AuditMark` keeps its prefix — measured
// against omniidl.  Second, diagnostics: `::Freight::AuditMark` is the name
// shape whose span used to cover the leading `::` and nothing else, which is
// how ~90 estate diagnostics came to advise qualifying `::` with `Module::::`
// (spikes/estate/, RC-2).  Here it resolves, so the shape is exercised on the
// success path too; the failure path is in the crate's own tests.
//
// 접두사 없는 루트가 인클루드된 타입을 `::` 정규화 이름으로 참조한다.
// 식별자와 진단 두 가지를 동시에 고정한다.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

#include "common.idl"

module Depot {

    interface Bay {

        ::Freight::AuditMark last_check();

        void record(in ::Freight::StampText note) raises (::Freight::NotFound);

    };

};
